WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.590
- I've heard you have had dwindlings

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:08.077
or little rumors of a presidential run?

00:00:08.077 --> 00:00:09.743
(Mark giggles)
- No.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:11.860
- No?
- No chance.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:12.919
- No chance?

00:00:12.919 --> 00:00:14.250
- None, none.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.940
How could you put your kids through that?

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.750
I could never put my children

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.210
through all the grief that happens

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:21.770
in a political campaign.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:23.600
Just not gonna happen, no.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.270
I actually considered it at one point

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.150
and we had a family vote.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.450
We did have a family vote.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.060
- So I'm not crazy?

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:30.893
- Well,

00:00:30.893 --> 00:00:32.362
- I mean, I know I am, but,

00:00:32.362 --> 00:00:33.450
(Mark and audience giggle)

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.972
you've thought about it?

00:00:34.972 --> 00:00:36.330
- There's five in our family

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:37.330
and the vote was four to one,

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:38.980
I was the only yes.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.370
So, yeah, the family doesn't agree,

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.080
it just can't happen.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.990
- I totally appreciate that.
(audience applauds)

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:47.506
That's why you'd make make
such a great president!

00:00:47.506 --> 00:00:48.690
(Mark giggles)

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:52.240
Okay, well, now, I was curious,

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.360
I was watching "Inventing Anna."

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.880
- Oh, I love that show.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.211
It's just insane.

00:00:57.211 --> 00:00:58.623
(audience applauds)

00:00:58.623 --> 00:01:01.086
It's just the craziest thing ever.

00:01:01.086 --> 00:01:03.980
- How does one pull off

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.500
getting people to invest and convince,

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.080
who is a complete fraud?

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:12.690
How do we Svengali our way into this?

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:15.200
What do you see when you
see a show like that?

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.820
- She made one big mistake.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.610
You can't steal.

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:19.840
That's the one thing you can't do.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:20.930
You can fake it till you make it,

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:22.890
but when she was ripping off the hotels,

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:25.870
when she would refuse to
pay back the credit card

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:26.703
for her friend,

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:30.010
if she had not done that,

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:33.260
she woulda ended up being in a great spot,

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:36.160
because even though she
didn't get her 281 Park

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:36.993
or whatever it was,

00:01:36.993 --> 00:01:39.300
and she didn't create her club,

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.560
and whether or not that was
a good idea, I don't know,

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.170
but everything else she did

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.180
was just networking and learning

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.630
and putting yourself in
a position to succeed.

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:50.940
And if she just had not ripped people off,

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:52.500
she'd be having conversations

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.867
with those same people saying,

00:01:53.867 --> 00:01:55.340
"You know what, that first thing,

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.245
the club didn't work,

00:01:57.245 --> 00:01:58.510
but let's talk about this",

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:00.050
and she'd have great
relationships with them.

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.470
But when you try to steal,

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:04.060
when you actually steal from somebody,

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.150
you go to jail and that's
exactly what she deserved.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.363
- And the karmic ladder, you cannot climb.

00:02:08.363 --> 00:02:09.996
- You cannot climb that ladder, right?

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:11.570
The karma, payback's a bitch,

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:13.483
and she she faced it.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.150
- Well, you are a favorite shark,

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:19.170
everybody loves you on that show,

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:20.590
it's so fun to watch you,

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.810
you learn, you get excited,

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.890
but gosh, if I have
this opportunity to ask,

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:30.740
what is one of your favorite
gets on "Shark Tank"?

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:33.490
And what is the one that got away?

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:35.570
- The one that got away was,

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:37.640
oh my goodness, Spikeball.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:40.073
People on the beach are always
playing, throwing it around,

00:02:40.073 --> 00:02:40.906
its great exercise,

00:02:40.906 --> 00:02:42.840
and they wanted to create a
league, a Spikeball league,

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.680
and have me be the commissioner.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.526
I did not want to be the commissioner

00:02:46.526 --> 00:02:47.726
of the Spikeball league,

00:02:47.726 --> 00:02:48.890
so that one got away
and they just blew up.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:51.070
One that I got that I'm really proud of

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.340
was a company called Cycloramic,

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.720
and what they did was, back
when the iPhone 5 was out,

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:57.860
they had an app

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:00.550
that when you put it on a
flat surface and started it,

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:02.310
it would take these panoramic pictures.

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:03.970
And I just thought that was really cool.

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:07.140
It became the number
one app in the app store

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.100
when "Shark Tank" aired,

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.950
and then iPhone changed
what it looked like,

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:12.500
so you couldn't just stand it up.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.050
So these guys had to pivot,

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:15.680
and they pivoted into something called

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.270
computer vision software,

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:20.300
and they turned into this
huge, enormous success.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:24.094
- Speaking of apps, I was
watching "Super Pumped."

00:03:24.094 --> 00:03:25.080
(Mark laughs)

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.510
The battle for Uber starring
Joseph Gordon-Levitt,

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.540
everybody get ready for
our next favorite show,

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:30.373
by the way.
- Amazing.

00:03:30.373 --> 00:03:31.707
- It's so good.
Amazing, yep.

00:03:31.707 --> 00:03:33.990
"Super Pumped" is great.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:34.890
- You're in it.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.360
- Yeah, I made my little appearance.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.193
- [Drew] Yes!

00:03:37.193 --> 00:03:38.363
- Yeah.

00:03:38.363 --> 00:03:41.120
- Is it true that you have
had anything to do with Uber

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.301
at one point or were considering it,

00:03:43.301 --> 00:03:44.134
and then,
- Considered.

00:03:44.134 --> 00:03:46.020
So Travis, the guy who started Uber,

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:47.456
- [Drew] Travis Kalanick?

00:03:47.456 --> 00:03:48.289
- Kalanick, yeah.

00:03:48.289 --> 00:03:50.290
So he had a company, Red
Swoosh, that I invested in.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.030
Then he comes to me with Uber

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:53.700
and I was one of the very first people,

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.130
it was called Uber Cab,

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:57.880
and Travis and I had this
love-hate relationship,

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.900
so I'm like, "Travis, I love the idea,

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:01.733
but you're gonna have all these problems,

00:04:01.733 --> 00:04:02.566
da, da, da, da, da,

00:04:02.566 --> 00:04:04.510
you're not raising enough
money, da, da, da, da, da."

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.450
And I went "Shark Tank" on 'em,

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:09.060
and didn't like the valuation.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.620
And he was like, "Fine",

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.090
and never called me back.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:12.923
So I had a chance

00:04:12.923 --> 00:04:15.820
to be one of the very
first investors in Uber

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:16.780
and I missed it.

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:20.500
- Okay, so there is a potential guy here

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:24.150
who might be "Shark Tank" material.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:27.010
Would you be so kind as to,

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:30.610
after the break, come
and meet him with me,

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:32.290
and see what his invention is?

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:34.150
- For you, Drew, I'll do anything.

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:36.110
- [Drew] Including run for
president one day with me?

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:37.484
- Almost anything.

00:04:37.484 --> 00:04:38.317
- Okay.

00:04:38.317 --> 00:04:39.939
All right, we'll be right back.

00:04:39.939 --> 00:04:42.522
(upbeat music)

